    turnFlow: 'The sneaker leads to the first trick; thereafter the winner of each trick leads to the next. Players must follow suit if possible, or trump if void in the led suit; when able they must head the trick (beat the current winning card). Four tricks are played per round. Each trick won pays one quarter of the pot (Pinke); a player who joins but takes no tricks pays a bête (equal to the pot); the sneaker with only one trick pays a bête, and with zero tricks pays double bête (Mauschelbete).',
